+/*
+ * ufsverify: compare what the device returns with what was just written (still in the bounce
+ * buffer). 1: plain read back (catches DMA/cache/LBA faults, can be served from the device's own
+ * write cache). 2: SYNCHRONIZE CACHE first, then a FUA read that has to come from the medium.
+ * A mismatch is reported and returned as EIO so the file system sees it.
